          "input": {
            "content": "Moves the whole AI SDK v6 line one step forward so every package agrees on the\nsame `@ai-sdk/provider` / `@ai-sdk/provider-utils` pair, and so the OpenAI\nadapter accepts the current reasoning-effort vocabulary.\n\n| package | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `ai` (catalog) | 6.0.217 | 6.0.256 |\n| `@ai-sdk/openai` | 3.0.79 | 3.0.97 |\n| `@ai-sdk/react` | 3.0.219 | 3.0.259 |\n| `@ai-sdk/mcp` (catalog) | 1.0.67 | 1.0.71 |\n| `@ai-sdk/provider` | 3.0.13 | 3.0.15 |\n| `@ai-sdk/provider-utils` | 4.0.34 | 4.0.46 |\n\n## Why these versions\n\n**`max` is now accepted on the Chat Completions path.** `@ai-sdk/openai@3.0.79`\nvalidates `providerOptions.openai.reasoningEffort` against a closed enum that\npredates OpenAI's current effort vocabulary:\n\n```js\n// 3.0.79\nreasoningEffort: z.enum([\"none\",\"minimal\",\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\",\"xhigh\"])\n// 3.0.97\nreasoningEffort: z.enum([\"none\",\"minimal\",\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\",\"xhigh\",\"max\"])\n```\n\n`parseProviderOptions` throws on a value outside that enum, so on 3.0.79 an\neffort of `max` fails for every provider routed through `openai.chat(...)` —\nthat is, every OpenAI-compatible endpoint, since `openai-model-client.ts`\nreserves the Responses path for `provider.id === \"openai\"`. The Responses\nschema is free-form `z.string().nullish()` and was unaffected either way.\n\n**The provider pair stops drifting.** `apps/api` pins `@ai-sdk/provider` and\n`@ai-sdk/provider-utils` to match `ai`'s own dependencies, but\n`@ai-sdk/mcp@1.0.67` already wanted `provider-utils@4.0.42` against `ai`'s\n`4.0.34`. At the versions in this PR all six packages resolve to\n`@ai-sdk/provider@3.0.15` and `@ai-sdk/provider-utils@4.0.46`.\n\n**Not the newest releases, deliberately.** `ai@6.0.264` / `@ai-sdk/openai@3.0.99`\nare 2 days old and fail the repository's `minimumReleaseAge: 10080` (7 day)\nsupply-chain cooldown. These are the newest versions that clear it (all\npublished 2026-08-14) and they carry the enum fix. No\n`minimumReleaseAgeExclude` entry was added.\n\n## Notes\n\n`@ai-sdk/mcp@1.0.71` declares no dependency or peer on\n`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, so the catalog's \"these two move together\" pairing\nwith `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.29.0` is unaffected and that pin is unchanged.\n\nLockfile churn is confined to the ai-sdk specifiers and their resolutions.\n\nFirst layer of the reasoning-effort stack: the proposal and implementation\nlayers above depend on `max` being sendable.\n",
